('advanced-native-171', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-171-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Persistent requests made refusing harder without changing the underlying wish."],"options":["Persistent requests made refusing harder without changing the underlying wish.","New evidence freely persuaded the speaker that joining was best.","The speaker had always been eager to join.","The phrase proves the speaker has already accepted."]},"advanced-native-171-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The repeated requests are exhausting me, so I need space to make a clear decision.","They have asked so often that saying no is becoming tiring.","The repeated calls are wearing down my resistance.","I feel pressured rather than genuinely interested."],"options":["The repeated requests are exhausting me, so I need space to make a clear decision.","They have asked so often that saying no is becoming tiring.","The repeated calls are wearing down my resistance.","I feel pressured rather than genuinely interested."]},"advanced-native-171-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The pressure is wearing down my resistance."],"options":["I have freely decided the product meets a need after new evidence.","The requests stopped after my first refusal, leaving me free to decide without further pressure.","The pressure is wearing down my resistance."]},"advanced-native-171-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Someone considers new evidence calmly and changes their opinion without pressure."],"options":["Someone considers new evidence calmly and changes their opinion without pressure.","Repeated pressure makes saying no increasingly difficult.","Constant requests make someone consider agreeing just to stop the demands."]},"advanced-native-171-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["You might wear down his resistance without changing what he wants. We should respect his refusal."],"options":["Repeat the request after the refusal and leave the discussion of preferences until later.","You might wear