('advanced-native-173', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-173-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["A post’s popularity and a person’s overall value."],"options":["A person with fewer likes has no value.","All information from audience response must be ignored.","A post’s popularity and a person’s overall value.","Popular posts and unpopular posts are always equally accurate."]},"advanced-native-173-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Likes are not reliable measures of self-worth.","People may not have seen the post, and their response is not a judgment on your whole life.","We can look at what you value beyond online reactions.","A number on one post does not define you as a person."],"options":["Likes are not reliable measures of self-worth.","People may not have seen the post, and their response is not a judgment on your whole life.","We can look at what you value beyond online reactions.","A number on one post does not define you as a person."]},"advanced-native-173-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Exam scores should not be our only measures of self-worth."],"options":["Scores can never give any information about learning.","Exam scores should not be our only measures of self-worth.","One low score proves a person has no value."]},"advanced-native-173-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["One popularity count fully determines someone’s value as a person."],"options":["One popularity count fully determines someone’s value as a person.","A grade can inform a learner about a particular performance.","A popularity count can provide limited feedback about a post."]},"advanced-native-173-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We can use feedback to learn without treating scores as complete measures of self-worth."],"options":["Leave the feedback unread because you do not want the score to define you.","Use the score to judge your value first, then look for the specific skills you can improve.","We can use feedback to learn without treating scores as complete measures