('advanced-native-175', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-175-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Readers may find it harder to distinguish two different kinds of content."],"options":["Readers may find it harder to distinguish two different kinds of content.","Advice and advertising have always been exactly the same.","Every reader has certainly been deceived already.","Labelling the content cannot help anyone understand its purpose."]},"advanced-native-175-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Clear information lets readers make a more informed judgment.","Readers should know when a recommendation is sponsored.","Without a label, it may blur the line between advice and advertising.","The label helps people evaluate the purpose of the message."],"options":["Clear information lets readers make a more informed judgment.","Readers should know when a recommendation is sponsored.","Without a label, it may blur the line between advice and advertising.","The label helps people evaluate the purpose of the message."]},"advanced-native-175-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The format may blur the line between personal advice and promotion."],"options":["The format makes the two purposes completely clear to everyone.","The format may blur the line between personal advice and promotion.","Readers are unsure only about when the product launched, not whether the piece is paid promotion."]},"advanced-native-175-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Sponsored content is clearly labelled and separated from independent guidance."],"options":["A paid promotion looks like an independent review without explanation.","Sponsored content is clearly labelled and separated from independent guidance.","A message combines a sales purpose with personal advice without making the payment clear."]},"advanced-native-175-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Knowing the author does not reveal the payment; an unlabelled recommendation can still blur the line between advice and advertising."],"optio